\subsection{QVD format notes}{

A QVD file has three sections:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{XML header}: metadata including field names, types, Qlik tags, and
layout parameters for the bit-packed data section.
\item \strong{Symbol table}: per-field dictionaries of all unique values, encoded
as typed entries (int32, double, or null-terminated string).
\item \strong{Data section}: a bit-packed record matrix where each row's fields are
encoded as variable-width indices into the symbol table.
}

The bit-extraction inner loop is implemented in C++ via \link[Rcpp:Rcpp-package]{Rcpp::Rcpp} for
performance. Reading a 1 million-row, 20-column QVD file typically
completes in 1–3 seconds on a modern machine.
}

